This is my fifth ascension, and the one that was the toughest
one yet.

I was looking through the files on an old computer the other day
and found an old save file. When i loaded it i found myself in the
Vault with a level 14 wizard. looking at the inventory i saw that i
had the bell and the Eye so i had obviously finished the quest.
On the other hand my equipment was only so so. I had cloak of
MR, Shield of reflection and gauntlets of power but only an crystal
platemail, rustproof iron shoes and a +0 rustproof dwarven helmet.
And i had no bag of holding either. And somehow i had managed
to get crowned somewhere on the way. At least i had most of
the necessary resistances, only missing disintegration.

So i collected all the tools and armour i could find and after some
polypiling i managed to get all my equipment rustproof and +4,
and completed with [BootsOfSpeed and [BagOfHolding. But i still
lacked a DSM of any kind.

I cleared down to the castle and in the castle a Black dragon was
kind enough to "give" me his black dragon scales. That gave me
the only resistance i was missing, disintegration.

After that it was an uneventful journey down to the Vibrating square.
Marked that and got the book from Rodney. Then the fun started.

I entered the sanctum and made my way to the altar there. It was
about then that Rodney decided to pay me a visit, and double trouble
me. Then one of the many monsters around me thought he needed
reinforcement and brought in Yeenoghu. A zap with a /WoDeath got
rid of one of the Rodneys. I was on #nethack on IRC and i mentioned
that i had 2 Rodneys and Yeenoghu beating at me. And thats when
someone on IRC said that now its only Demogorgon that's missing.
And of course thats the moment when Yeenoghu thought he needed
some help and brought in, you guessed it, Demogorgon! Thanks to
a =RoConflict Demogorgon  beat up on Yeenoughu enough for him to
escape upstairs. /oDeath took care of the second Rodney and then it
was just me and Demogorgon left. I managed to Kill him but only after
being poisoned to the brink of death. My blessed Unicorn horn failed
twice in a row,  luckily it worked the third time. After i had
finished that
fight i just left my computer and sat staring at a wall for 10 minutes
to
collect myself. :) Thats the first time i have had 2 Rodneys,
Yeenoghu
and Demogorgon at the same time. And its not an experience i want
to try again anytime soon. :)

On the way up Rodney annoyed  me more than he usually does. He
appeared at least six or seven times before i even had left Gehennon,
 and EVERY time he double troubled me. And he escaped up stairs
and used wands of digging so i had to follow him up or down several
times. I was out of /WoDeaths by that point so the trip from the
Sanctum to the dungeon levels took a really long time. I think the
only
time he did not double trouble me was for his final appearance in the
plane of earth. When i finally was at the stairs i had one real "AoY
and
five cheap plastic imitations!

Then it was time to go up through the astral planes. I managed to die
once on the plane of air thanks to not watching my hunger and being
swallowed by an air elemental. I just was in too much of a hurry to
get to the portal and get out of there i guess.

After that the Astral plane felt almost easy. The only drawback was
that by Bag of holding got cursed so i had to drop it. That was
because
i had switched from Magicbane to Stormbringer. So i lost a bit of
equipment there, and a lot of diamonds.

Offered the Amulet and....

